  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "How to read this",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 7
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### Metric \u2192 trace \u2192 logs, in three clicks\n\n1. **Latency panel** (left): hover a diamond. That is an *exemplar* \u2014 one real request in that histogram bucket, carrying its `trace_id`. Click **Query with Tempo**.\n2. **Trace view**: the trace runs `POST /orders` \u2192 `orders send` \u2192 `orders process` (worker) \u2192 `GET /internal/pricing` (api again), with the queue hop shown as a link from the consumer span to the producer span. Click a span, then **Logs for this span**.\n3. **Logs**: every line the two services wrote under that trace, filtered by `trace_id` structured metadata \u2014 not a text search. Each line has a **View trace** button back.\n\nRun `./scripts/break-it.sh` for slow (`SLOW-*`) and failing (`FAIL-*`) orders: they are always kept by tail sampling and show up as red spans and 5xx exemplars.\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "api latency p95 with exemplars",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 7,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 9
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(http_server_request_duration_seconds_bucket{service=\"api\"}[1m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p95",
          "exemplar": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {}
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "worker job duration p95 with exemplars",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 7,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 9
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(queue_job_duration_seconds_bucket{queue=\"orders\"}[1m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p95",
          "exemplar": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {}
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Recent traces that crossed the queue (TraceQL)",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "tempo",
        "uid": "tempo"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 16,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 10
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "tempo",
            "uid": "tempo"
          },
          "queryType": "traceql",
          "query": "{ span.messaging.system = \"bullmq\" && kind = consumer }",
          "limit": 20,
          "tableType": "traces"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {},
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {},
      "description": "Consumer spans from the worker; open one to see the whole trace including the producer side in the api."
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "logs",
      "title": "Log lines with a trace id",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "loki"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 16,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 10
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "loki"
          },
          "expr": "{service=~\"api|worker\"} | trace_id != \"\""
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {},
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "showTime": true,
        "wrapLogMessage": false,
        "enableLogDetails": true,
        "dedupStrategy": "none",
        "sortOrder": "Descending"
      },
      "description": "Expand a line: trace_id and span_id are structured metadata, and the trace_id field carries a link to Tempo."
    }
  ]
}